Phasmid: WebGPU adapter

What:     requestAdapter() resolves to the profile's adapter: GPUAdapterInfo
          vendor, architecture, device, description, subgroup sizes, the ids,
          features and limits come from gpu.webgpu, set where the GPU
          process's wire server answers the renderer; isFallbackAdapter is
          false. Without a hardware adapter (headless, Xvfb, no GPU) the
          SwiftShader Vulkan fallback backs the claim, without
          --enable-unsafe-webgpu; forceFallbackAdapter still gets null.
          Requiring a listed feature or limit the backing adapter lacks fails
          as a disallowed feature or limit. available false resolves null;
          getPreferredCanvasFormat() reports preferred_canvas_format.
          backendType and adapterType stay the host's. Unbacked claims are
          logged.
Why:      WebGPU must describe the same GPU as WebGL, in every mode.
Profile:  gpu.webgpu.available, vendor, architecture, device, description,
          subgroup_min_size, subgroup_max_size, features, limits,
          preferred_canvas_format; gpu.vendor_id, gpu.device_id
Hooks:    gpu/command_buffer/service/webgpu_decoder_impl.cc (constructor,
          IsFeatureExposed, RequestAdapterImpl, AdapterGetFeaturesImpl,
          RequestDeviceImpl, CreatePreferredAdapter, CanUseAdapter); new
          phasmid_webgpu.{h,cc}; third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgpu/
          gpu.cc (GPU::getPreferredCanvasFormat), gpu_adapter.cc
          (CreateAdapterInfoForAdapter)
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker; headless and
          headful
Guard:    tests/guards/graphics/webgpu.py

